// A field whose type names another model this same file declares has a type the
// file states: the name written beside the field. `declaredFieldType` answered
// only a builtin, so in `o.i.n` the read of `i` stayed `unknown` and the read
// under it could never be reached -- E2004 reported both, and the file's
// canonical text was suppressed by a type the source spells.
//
// The answer is the written name, not the model it resolves to. The language
// accepts `model Node { value: int  next: Node }` today
// (tests/suite/model_local_named_mid.orb), so a resolution that chased a leaf
// has no bound to stop at; the chain's depth comes from the AST, one table
// lookup per hop.
import "../../compiler/tir/entry.orb"

fn main() {
    val source = "model Inner { n: int }  model Outer { i: Inner }  fn f(o: Outer) -> int { return o.i.n }"
    print(compileFrontendSource("fixture", source))
}
